From: ENIAC Touch Kiosk <kiosk@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] accumulator: serialize the 1PP correction with receives

The cycling unit's pulses are fanned out to every unit concurrently
(fanout() in eniac.go). At 1PP time an accumulator whose receive program
has the correct switch set (cc C) increments its own units digit in
doonepp() (accunit goroutine), while a subtracting transmitter's 1' pulse
for the same accumulator arrives through accunit2() -> accrecv(), which
increments the same digit in another goroutine. Both are unsynchronized
read-modify-writes of u.val[0], so now and then one increment is lost.
trajdemo.e then punches cards whose last field is a few units off from
some card on (anywhere from card 2 to card 18 in our runs, about 1 run in
3 on a Mac); the race detector reports accrecv vs doonepp. A per-unit
mutex around both updates makes the output identical run to run (12 of
12 runs, including 8 at once). Spike #31; reported upstream (see #34).
Drop this patch once upstream fixes it.

---
diff --git a/src/accumulator.go b/src/accumulator.go
--- a/src/accumulator.go
+++ b/src/accumulator.go
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ package main
 import (
 	"fmt"
 	"strconv"
+	"sync"
 )
 
 /*
@@ -69,6 +70,7 @@ type accumulator struct {
 	whichrp             bool
 	change              chan int
 	lbuddy, rbuddy      int
+	mu                  sync.Mutex // val, decff, sign: accrecv vs the 1PP correction
 }
 
 var units [20]accumulator
@@ -383,6 +385,8 @@ func st2(unit int) int {
 
 func accrecv(unit, dat int) {
 	u := &units[unit]
+	u.mu.Lock()
+	defer u.mu.Unlock()
 	for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
 		if dat&1 == 1 {
 			u.val[i]++
@@ -558,11 +562,13 @@ func doonepp(u *accumulator, unit int, resp chan int) {
 		 * Connection of PX-5-109 pins 14, 15
 		 */
 		if u.rbuddy == unit {
+			u.mu.Lock()
 			u.val[0]++
 			if u.val[0] > 9 {
 				u.val[0] = 0
 				u.decff[0] = true
 			}
+			u.mu.Unlock()
 		}
 	}
 	if curprog&(stAS|stS) != 0 && u.S != nil {
